\paragraph{Why does generation degrade at repo level?} Output complexity increases nonlinearly: function-level outputs average ${\sim}$5--15 tokens; repo-level outputs average ${\sim}$477 tokens (Figure~\ref{fig:cwm_unparseable}), leading to format collapse under our ${\leq}$8B LoRA protocol (53--74\% unparseable; representative error examples in Appendix~\ref{app:qualitative}).

